{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-140044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $det(A)-3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero row, we obtain:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-3det(B)=0-3\\cdot 0=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-140044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-144"] ["math" "-72"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "72"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $2det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1)=5\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+3det(B)=2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-42958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "10\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=(-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=-\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-82286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ only"] ["text" "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only"] ["text" "$|B|$ only"] ["text" "$|C|$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$|B|$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The $A$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|A|=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1\\cdot 4=8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(C)=5\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot (-10)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-140046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ only"] ["text" "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only"] ["text" "$|B|$ only"] ["text" "$|C|$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|B|=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 5=-15\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-42959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$"] ["text" "$|B|$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $4det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4det(A)+4det(B)=4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 0=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-42459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42882" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-42882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$"] ["text" "$|B|$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42882" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|B|=-1\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-2det(B)=0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140047" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-140047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140047" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 4=-40\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-43058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only"] ["text" "$|A|$ only"] ["text" "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only"] ["text" "$|C|$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $3det(A)-4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=7\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 4=-5.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-4det(B)=3\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 0=-15.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-42467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-15"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has a zero row\n- $A$ has two proportional columns\n- $A$ has two identical rows" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero row.\n\n- $A$ has two proportional columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-42460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has identical rows" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-140050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-140050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- $A$ has two identical columns" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor two identical columns.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-43306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-43306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- $A$ has two identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-82290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/ac