3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "098c907827027c9ba8c4f54f94c0f3b2b948326175b48be7e46db2e598bad739"} {"question" "q-42458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "q-42458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/state.json" "file_sha256" "b143b4d13f81a87c52d43e60ab496340ab017c6cd5ecba632025a002a44e16ad"} {"question" "e-10994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $5\\det(A)-\\det(B),$ where \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/65df227e4fff9e934cec11be0a0262a1093a82270f3c9b0b7970fa2c700151aa.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/example-10994.json" "file_sha256" "722a8de0676a07a309da8daab2633115887640446a22b819e41a0e32850b68f7"} {"question" "e-10994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/23865048a3c2ad60dd3b51fe78c44ee368692172300814c3fb061f447266e233.png)\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\det(B) = 3 \\cdot (-4) \\cdot (-2) = 24\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5\\det(A)-\\det(B) = 5 \\cdot 0 - 24 = -24.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/example-10994.json" "file_sha256" "722a8de0676a07a309da8daab2633115887640446a22b819e41a0e32850b68f7"} {"question" "e-10995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/d95e60cbfa50178878e719166ace3dbff90c3cc5531acfc046d8354320cd4b00.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/example-10995.json" "file_sha256" "788cf6b695cda82d0b1f122c4bbe46f0b8ce6378cd76fde81f6ac8e9b0bef223"} {"question" "e-10995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/3f434912c97c20d04f703253fe41c169497cae82657cfbd0d8b548985549fe64.png)\nAs a result, $|A| = 0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, so \n\n$$\n|B| = (-1) \\cdot 4 \\cdot (-3) = 12 \\neq 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/5f41ff4f7fe5aeae5865bef9ab16d5d97a3513277f70b797c4167882093ed079.png)\nAs a result, $|C| = 0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/example-10995.json" "file_sha256" "788cf6b695cda82d0b1f122c4bbe46f0b8ce6378cd76fde81f6ac8e9b0bef223"} {"question" "e-10996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/ccc50eec6218625f22e8372d6f0b1dbf0da0aa921dff237e4e1b8ea3761bdfc7.png)\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0.$\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows\n\n- $A$ has identical columns" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/example-10996.json" "file_sha256" "72bda62d184b3899aa9a5ba754b5a338d06004bf39a78d7066eaa18e767c9ce8"} {"question" "e-10996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/2a155f75e1e9c099540eeac555cb20fde5037837d9e5fc9f976bbca15369b51e.png)\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/1447045fa5b7875defffdf52d2ae8cf876ee0c5da6ac07cc37bc1c5525fec9c6.png)\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/example-10996.json" "file_sha256" "72bda62d184b3899aa9a5ba754b5a338d06004bf39a78d7066eaa18e767c9ce8"}] "usage" {"q-42959" [] "e-10996" [] "q-42458" [] "q-42882" [] "q-43306" [] "q-42459" [] "e-10994" [] "e-10995" []} "basis" 1725 "retractions" [[17592186134333 :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0$?\n\n$\\begin{vmatrix}A|= & 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}1; \\sqrt{5}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}0\\begin{vmatrix}, & B|= & 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix}0; 0\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}5\\begin{vmatrix}, & C|= & 4 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix}4; 2\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix}1 \\mid$"] [17592186134319 :question/problem "Find $4det(A) + 4det(B)$, where\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186134332 :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0$?\n\n$\\begin{vmatrix}A|= & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{3}; \\sqrt[5]{2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}0\\begin{vmatrix}, & B|= & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}4; 0\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}4\\begin{vmatrix}, & C|= & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}4; 2\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}4 \\mid$"] [17592186134339 :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix such that $\\mid A|= 0$. Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n1. $A$ has two identical rows\n2. One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n3. $A$ has two identical columns"] [17592186134318 :question/problem "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $\\mid A|= 0$?\n\n1. $A$ has a zero column\n2. $A$ has identical columns\n3. $A$ has identical rows"] [17592186133390 :question/problem "Find $5\\det(A)-\\det(B)$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & \\sqrt{13} & 4 \\\\ 4 & 11 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 9 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186133390 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & \\sqrt{13} & 4 \\\\ 4 & 11 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 9 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n$\\det(B) = 3 \\cdot (-4) \\cdot (-2) = 24$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5\\det(A)-\\det(B) = 5 \\cdot 0 - 24 = -24\n$$"] [17592186133391 :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0$?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186133391 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nAs a result, $\\mid A \\mid = 0$.\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, so\n$\\mid B \\mid = (-1) \\cdot 4 \\cdot (-3) = 12 \\neq 0$.\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nAs a result, $\\mid C \\mid = 0$.\n\nTherefore, only $\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid C \\mid$ are equal to $0$."] [17592186133392 :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $\\mid A|=0$.\n\n1. $A$ has a zero column\n2. $A$ has proportional rows\n3. $A$ has identical columns"] [17592186133392 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- $A$ has proportional rows:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""]] "immutable_answers" [17592186132351 17592186132352 17592186132353 17592186132354 17592186132355 17592186132357 17592186132358 17592186132359 17592186132360 17592186132361 17592186132435 17592186132436 17592186132437 17592186132438 17592186132439 17592186132441 17592186132442 17592186132443 17592186132444 17592186132445 17592186132477 17592186132478 17592186132479 17592186132480 17592186132481] "immutable_fields" [[17592186132350 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132350 :answer-field/id] [17592186132350 :answer-field/key] [17592186132350 :answer-field/type] [17592186132356 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132356 :answer-field/id] [17592186132356 :answer-field/key] [17592186132356 :answer-field/type] [17592186132434 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132434 :answer-field/id] [17592186132434 :answer-field/key] [17592186132434 :answer-field/type] [17592186132440 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132440 :answer-field/id] [17592186132440 :answer-field/key] [17592186132440 :answer-field/type] [17592186132476 :answer-field/correct] [17592186132476 :answer-field/id] [17592186132476 :answer-field/key] [17592186132476 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
